 3. 🪖 U.S. strikes Iranian mine launchers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Ships are anchored in the Strait of Hormuz. Photo: Ali Saeedi/Getty Images The U.S. military struck Iranian military targets to prevent the deployment of sea mines in the Strait of Hormuz, a U.S. official told Axios' Barak Ravid. 

 Why it matters: This is the first known U.S. strike in Iran since late July. Iran retaliated with limited attacks on both the UAE and Jordan.

 Oil surged 3% after the exchange of fire. Threat level: President Trump posted an apparent AI video overnight that he said showed Iran's crucial Kharg Island oil terminal being "blown to smithereens."

 Seizing or destroying Kharg, the heart of Iran's oil industry, has been one of his regular threats during the war. The U.S. military last week finished clearing all mines from the strait's main shipping lane.

 Trump said then that Iran was notified that any ship or boat placing new mines would be "immediately and systematically destroyed." Keep reading . 

 
 
