 4. 🥳 Happy 50th to the first index fund 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The OG stock index fund, the Vanguard 500, turns 50 years old today.

 Why it matters: Passive funds ate the world. Today, index funds make up 64% of all stock fund assets, and millions of investors use them, Axios markets correspondent Emily Peck writes. Most of us are socking away money in these things automatically through 401(k) payroll deductions.

 Stat du jour: If you'd put $10,000 in the Vanguard 500 back in 1976, it'd be worth over $2 million today. Get Axios Markets . 

 
 
