 8. 🎥 1 film thing: Wile E. Coyote&#x27;s back 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Wile E. Coyote, voiced by Eric Bauza, in "Coyote vs. Acme." Photo: Ketchup Entertainment via AP The abrupt termination of "Coyote vs. Acme" sent shockwaves through Hollywood. 

 Everyone in the movie business is accustomed to sudden, painful twists of fate. But the wholesale elimination of a finished film faster than you can say "Meep! Meep!" was something new. But nearly three years later, the movie is, like its ever-undaunted protagonist, back from the dead.

 After an outcry, Warner Bros. put "Coyote vs. Acme" up for sale. Ketchup Entertainment, an independent distributor that last year released the Looney Tunes movie "The Day the Earth Blew Up," picked it up for about $50 million. Now it's in theaters. The movie opened with a respectable $15 million box-office haul, second only to the juggernaut that is "Spider-Man."

